  "$comment": "Vendored binaries and pinned images (PLAN §9.1). Binaries are shipped byte-identical (never re-signed); every value here is verified before use. packaging/build-app.ts downloads each archive, checks size and sha256, copies the contents byte-identically (so the vendors' own code signatures stay valid) and checks teamId on every extracted Mach-O. container.installRootFiles is what the bundled install root must hold (the PC manager's isProvisioned() checks it). lume.appFiles is the notarized lume.app byte for byte (provisioned for dev under MineVibe-dev/lume, checked with codesign and spctl, never re-signed); images.cua-macos pins the macOS image by tag and manifest digest (Lume records the pulled digest in <vm>/.manifest-digest). Bump a pin only after checking the new archive by hand (packaging/README.md, spikes/s5-container/result.md).",
